        "faq-1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes Farm Dip Pure Desi Buffalo Ghee special?",
            "answer": "<p>Made from pure buffalo milk, it has a rich, creamy texture, authentic taste and delicious flavour that makes every meal special. It is 100% natural with no preservatives or additives.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is buffalo ghee white?",
            "answer": "<p>Buffalo milk carries very little beta-carotene, the pigment that makes cow ghee yellow. So pure buffalo ghee is naturally creamy white. The colour is not a sign of anything added or removed.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does Farm Dip ghee have any preservatives or additives?",
            "answer": "<p>No. It is ghee made from pure buffalo milk and nothing else: no preservatives, no additives, no colour.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is my ghee solid, or grainy?",
            "answer": "<p>Buffalo ghee sets firm in cool weather and softens in summer, and it is often a mix of the two. The texture changes with temperature and does not change the quality.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which pack size should I buy?",
            "answer": "<p>The 500 ml jar (₹1,350) suits small families or a first try. The 1 L jar (₹2,210) is the most popular monthly staple. For joint families, the 5 L jar (₹9,900) costs the least per litre, at ₹2,220.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is buffalo ghee good for everyday cooking?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. It is rich and holds up well to high heat, which makes it good for tadka, parathas, puris and frying, and for traditional sweets like halwa and ladoo.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
